From 669859c1a8fa2a27ba2abf70b74373b5d64da913 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Claude (stage1 experiment)" <leeyoonjae2002@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 15:01:09 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] feat(lidar): add opt-in track trace, competition replay
 inputs and tracking frame options

Stage-1 diagnosis instrumentation and two default-off tracking options on top of P0
(916e4d9e + replay harness 39cffc57). With every option off and no trace path the
tracker output is unchanged (verified by replay identity against the P0 run).

- Lidar/Tracking/TrackTrace.hpp: bounded, buffered JSONL track trace (default off),
  per-track selection; tracking_options::reacquire_elapsed_init and
  tracking_options::ego_translation_comp switches.
- Tracking/Kalman/FrameBoundary/LidarProcess: trace hooks (detections, merges,
  association candidates, KF prior/innovation/gain/posterior, OBB stabilisation
  before/after, births, misses, retire, drop, scan inputs and stage times).
- reacquire_elapsed_init: second-observation velocity divides by the time elapsed
  since the first observation instead of the last scan dt (P0 gives (k+1)x speed
  after k missed scans).
- ego_translation_comp: common-geometry frame alignment also removes the base_link
  arc from vel_x and IMU yaw, so the KF velocity is ground referenced and the CAN
  speed is no longer added to it.
- main.cpp: ConfigureTrackingExperiment() reads the switches and trace params.
- lidar_dataset_replay: --input-mode competition (reads only vel_x and IMU
  attitude columns, feeds no GPS), --track-trace, publish/planner trace records.
- test_tracking_frame_options: cause tests on ideal measurements through the
  production FrameFilter chain (fail with the options off, pass with them on).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
